# LeakSanitizer suppressions for spudaudio_test on Linux, under the -asan
# presets (set on the test in CMakeLists.txt). Third-party code only, each
# with its reason; SpudLib's own leaks are fixed, never listed here.

# PipeWire, loaded by ALSA's pipewire PCM plugin (the default device on a
# PipeWire desktop) inside snd_pcm_open: pw_context_new loads its modules
# and keeps allocations that snd_pcm_close never frees; the modules are
# unloaded by then, so most frames read "<unknown module>". SpudAudio closes
# every PCM it opens (spudaudioalsa.c, alsa_open and its callers). Seen
# 2026-10-25 on Fedora 44, PipeWire 1.6.9, alsa-lib 1.2.16.
leak:pw_context_load_module
